# Deploy to /etc/systemd/system/wsl-mount-guard.service
#
# Why this exists: /mnt/wsl is a tmpfs SHARED by every distro in the WSL VM, so
# mount propagation runs in both directions. When another distro shuts down
# gracefully, its systemd unmounts the propagated copies it holds under
# /mnt/wsl, and those unmounts propagate back here and take THIS distro's own
# bind with them. Measured: the local mount unit deactivates about six seconds
# after the peer's. `wsl --terminate` does not do this -- a hard kill never runs
# the graceful unmount path, the same split that no-unregister.conf is written
# around.
#
# The /etc/fstab entry only re-establishes the bind at OUR boot, so once a peer
# has taken it down nothing puts it back until the next restart. This timer is
# what puts it back.
#
# Targets are read out of /etc/fstab rather than hardcoded, so the same unit
# file works in every distro with no per-distro substitution. The check is
# surgical on purpose -- it only mounts a target that is currently absent, so it
# never disturbs a live mount or anything else under /mnt/wsl.
#
# mkdir is safe here in a way it is NOT safe in fstab: this runs well after the
# shared tmpfs is in place. Creating the mount point from an fstab option
# (X-mount.mkdir) instead lands it in the pre-tmpfs directory that WSL's early
# `mount -a` sees, and the real tmpfs then buries the result as an unreachable
# orphan. See agent/skills/wsl-windows-command/references/cross-distro.md.
#
# Two syntax notes for anyone editing the ExecStart line. $$ is a literal dollar
# sign -- systemd expands $NAME there, so a shell variable has to be doubled.
# And the comment pattern is written "#"* rather than \#* because systemd warns
# "Ignoring unknown escape sequences" on the backslash form. Skipping comment
# lines is not optional: the fstab block above contains lines whose second field
# is a real /mnt/wsl path inside prose, and those would otherwise be mounted.
[Unit]
Description=Re-establish this distro's /mnt/wsl bind mounts if they went missing
Documentation=man:systemd.mount(5) man:fstab(5)
ConditionPathIsMountPoint=/mnt/wsl

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/bin/sh -c 'while read -r src tgt rest; do case "$$src" in "#"*) continue ;; esac; case "$$tgt" in /mnt/wsl/*) ;; *) continue ;; esac; mountpoint -q "$$tgt" || { mkdir -p "$$tgt"; mount "$$tgt"; }; done < /etc/fstab'
